# ShareGo project context

ShareGo sends a short secret between exactly 2 devices on the same Wi-Fi. There is no server and no relay.

## Stack

One Flutter app in this repository. It builds Android, iOS, macOS, Windows, and Linux. There is no React Native and no Electron.

## Invariants

1. No cloud, TURN, signaling, or relay
2. Same local network only
3. Exactly 2 participants, no late join
4. Receiver listens, sender connects, receiver approves
5. Crypto goes through the `cryptography` package (X25519, HKDF-SHA256, XChaCha20-Poly1305)
6. Ephemeral keys only. Never persist secrets
7. QR and the 6-character code are bootstrap only
8. The code and keys regenerate every 30 seconds until a valid handshake
9. User-facing text lives in `lib/strings.dart`
10. Timeouts and limits live in `lib/config.dart`

## Layout

- `lib/core/crypto.dart` — key agreement, derivation, encrypt, decrypt, wipe
- `lib/core/frames.dart` — length-prefixed TCP frames
- `lib/core/protocol.dart` — messages, QR payload, code format
- `lib/core/session.dart` — receiver and sender
- `lib/core/discovery.dart` — mDNS, with typed-address fallback
- `lib/ui/` — screens
- `docs/` — protocol, architecture, threat model, building

Comments are lowercase and only explain why. The version is `version` in `pubspec.yaml`.
